5.1 L7 Deep Protocol Dissector

Inspect the implementation of QUIC, SSH, SMB2/3 and HTTP/2 analysis.

For every supported protocol, determine exactly what the parser can and cannot establish from the provided packet bytes.

Verify:

Bounds checking before every read.

Correct offset and length validation.

Handling of truncated data.

Handling of malformed length fields.

Correct endianness.

Valid and invalid protocol signatures.

Unknown protocol versions.

Empty input.

Minimum-size input.

Excessively large input.

Repeated calls with different buffers.

No shared mutable parsing state leaking between requests.

No uncaught exceptions on adversarial packets.

For QUIC, verify header-form distinctions, version fields, connection IDs and packet-type interpretation against appropriate protocol specifications and test fixtures.

Do not imply that encrypted QUIC payloads can be decoded into application data without the required keys and supported decryption capabilities.

For SSH fingerprinting, verify which message fields are available, how the fingerprint is calculated, how missing algorithm lists are treated, and which hash variants are implemented. Do not describe an arbitrary banner hash as an authenticated SSH client identity.

For SMB2/3, verify structural parsing, message types, flags and supported header fields. Distinguish observed protocol features or suspicious access patterns from proof of malicious lateral movement.

For HTTP/2, validate the client preface, frame boundaries, frame lengths and malformed data. Make it clear when the parser sees only a partial frame or encrypted transport traffic.

